    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56558" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κενεμβᾰτ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>step on emptiness</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Flam.</u>
				10
			</span></i>; <i>step into a hole</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(2).887
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Gall.</u>
				26
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Medic., of a
			lancet, catheter, etc., <i>reach a cavity</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				44.11.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.786
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				6.59
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>lack solid foundation</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κενεμβατοῦν καὶ σφαλλόμενον</span>, of Alexander's
			Empire, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.336f
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κενεμβατοῦμεν ταῦτα λέγοντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dam.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				3.9.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>lead a frivolous life</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.Prot.
				p.2
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i></div>
